## Control {{controlId}}: Ensure Equipment Removed for Off-Site Maintenance Is Sanitized of Any CUI

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization sanitizes CUI from equipment before off-site maintenance within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through data sanitization procedures and encryption enforcement documented in "Equipment Sanitization Policy v1.0" maintained by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if bitLockerEnforced}}
**Encryption-Based Protection:**
BitLocker Drive Encryption on {{deviceCount}} managed devices ensures CUI is cryptographically inaccessible even if equipment is sent for off-site maintenance without full sanitization. Recovery keys are stored in Entra ID and are not shared with maintenance vendors.
{{/if}}

**Sanitization Procedures:**
- **Cloud-First Architecture:** CUI primarily resides in M365 GCC High cloud services, minimizing local data on devices sent for maintenance
- **Pre-Maintenance Sanitization:** Before off-site maintenance, devices are wiped of locally cached CUI using Intune remote wipe or manual NIST SP 800-88 Clear/Purge procedures
- **Verification:** Sanitization verified by {{variables.systemAdministrator}} before equipment release to maintenance vendor
- **Documentation:** Sanitization certificate completed with device identifier, sanitization method, verification results, and date

{{#if pimConfigured}}
**Maintenance Access Controls:**
PIM ensures that administrative credentials are not stored on devices sent for maintenance — just-in-time activation means no persistent privileged tokens exist on the device.
{{/if}}

**Operational Procedure:**
- **Action:** Sanitize CUI from equipment before off-site release; document sanitization; verify before handoff
- **Frequency:** Per maintenance event
- **Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}
- **Documentation:** Equipment Sanitization Policy v1.0, Sanitization Certificate Form MA-003

**Review Frequency:** Per event, quarterly audit by ISSO

**Verification Method:** Examine sanitization certificates, equipment maintenance logs, Intune wipe records, and vendor maintenance documentation.

